<BaseLayout title="Pradeep Badekkila — Founder of REVERB Inc." description="Meet Pradeep Badekkila, multilingual voice artist, television and radio presenter, Namma Metro voice and founder of REVERB Inc." {schema}><section class="page-hero"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/about/">About</a> / Pradeep Badekkila</div><h1>Pradeep <em>Badekkila.</em></h1><p>Some voices you hear. His, you recognize.</p></section><section class="section"><div class="founder-grid"><img class="founder-photo" src="/images/pradeep-badekkila-transparent.png" srcset="/images/pradeep-badekkila-transparent-640.png 640w, /images/pradeep-badekkila-transparent.png 1024w" sizes="(max-width: 800px) 90vw, 38vw" alt="Pradeep Badekkila, founder of REVERB Inc." width="1024" height="1280" decoding="async"/><div class="founder-copy"><h2>Twenty years between a language and the person listening.</h2><p>For twenty years, Pradeep Badekkila has lived inside the space between a language and the person listening to it—as a multilingual voice artist, producer, and presenter across television and radio, and as the voice that guides millions of Bengaluru commuters home every day on Namma Metro.</p><p>REVERB Inc. is what that career became: a studio built on the belief that a good voice-over isn&rsquo;t translated, it&rsquo;s <em>felt</em>—in whichever of India&rsquo;s languages an audience calls their own.</p><a class="text-link" href="/contact/">Start a conversation →</a></div></div></section></BaseLayout>
